# PinballWizard Phase 4.5 evaluation ground-truth (v2, realigned 2026-06-09).
# See data/eval/README.md for the format and curation conventions.
# Citation IDs are raw OPDB ids (e.g. "GweeP-Ml9pZ"), not prefixed —
# AiRouter.ExtractCitationsFromText extracts these from the
# https://opdb.org/machines/<id> URL pattern in the agent's text.
#
# Edition-aware fields (AB#259, edition-scope-model-design §6):
#   acceptable_citation_sets : any-of list of acceptable citation sets;
#                              a prediction matching ANY set scores correct.
#   franchise_wide_ok        : true => a franchise-wide doc cited for any
#                              edition is acceptable (limitation: Citation
#                              carries no edition_scope yet, so this is the
#                              row-level intent, not a per-citation check).
#   expected_outcome         : grounded | answered_all_editions (R2) |
#                              honest_substitution (R3). Default grounded.
#   required_editions        : R2 => each label must appear attributed;
#                              R3 => [0] is the named edition the disclosure
#                              must reference.
#
# v2 changes vs v1 (2026-06-09):
#   - Foo Fighters: added GpeoL-MyNPq to acceptable_citation_sets for all
#     Foo Fighters questions; post-migration index has two FF IDs (191
#     chunks each). Either ID is an acceptable ground-truth citation.
#   - JJP Toy Story 4: changed acceptable_refusal to true for ev-rules-0005,
#     ev-valuation-0005, ev-repair-0005. The index has only 1 chunk for
#     GJ2o0-MrRye (OPDB metadata card only — no manual/document content
#     indexed), making grounded answers impossible with current corpus.
#     Treat refusal as correct until content is indexed.
#   - Header comment: added GpeoL-MyNPq to OPDB ID table.
#
# 30 questions: 24 graded + 6 acceptable-refusal (was 27+3; JJP moved).
# All graded questions target the 6 remaining Phase 4 curated-subset
# machines with adequate indexed content.
#
# Distribution (graded):
#   Godzilla (Stern, edition-aware)  — 2 Rules + 2 Valuation + 2 Repair (AB#259: R1/R2/R3)
#   Foo Fighters LE (Stern)         — 2 Rules + 2 Valuation + 2 Repair
#   Toy Story 4 (JJP)               — 0 graded (1-chunk index gap → acceptable_refusal)
#   Galactic Tank Force (AP)        — 1 Rules + 1 Valuation + 1 Repair
#   Halloween (Spooky)              — 1 Rules + 1 Valuation + 1 Repair
#   Attack from Mars Remake (CGC)   — 1 Rules + 1 Valuation + 1 Repair
#   Queen LE (Pinball Brothers)     — 1 Rules + 1 Valuation + 1 Repair
#
# OPDB IDs used:
#   GweeP-MW95j  Stern | Godzilla (Pro)         — AB#259 edition-aware base
#   GweeP-Ml9pZ  Stern | Godzilla (Premium/LE)
#   GpeoL-MkPz1  Stern | Foo Fighters (Premium/LE) — post-migration ID 1
#   GpeoL-MyNPq  Stern | Foo Fighters (Premium/LE) — post-migration ID 2 (191 chunks)
#   GJ2o0-MrRye  Jersey Jack Pinball | Toy Story 4 — 1 chunk only; refusal acceptable
#   Gj6PZ-Mb5z6  American Pinball | Galactic Tank Force
#   Gj66Z-Mp4BN  Spooky Pinball | Halloween
#   G4do5-MkPnV  Chicago Gaming | Attack From Mars (Remake)
#   GELkO-Ml9zZ  Pinball Brothers | Queen

